 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Retract stability of complex weights",
 "statement": "Every direct summand of an object of $D_{\\le w}(X_0)$ again belongs to\n$D_{\\le w}(X_0)$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-d-dl-general-weights/lem-zl-complex-retract.md",
  "place": "node lem-zl-complex-retract, order 2813"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-derived-cohomology-sheaves"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "If $K=K'\\oplus K''$, then\n$\\mathcal H^j(K)=\\mathcal H^j(K')\\oplus\\mathcal H^j(K'')$ (cohomology\nof a direct sum), so each cohomology sheaf of the summand is a direct\nsummand of a cohomology sheaf of $K$, which is $\\iota$-mixed of\nweights at most $w+j$ by [def-weil-complex-weights]; by the\nmixedness for direct summands of [lem-a1-mixed-direct-summand],\n$\\mathcal H^j(K')$ is $\\iota$-mixed of weights at most $w+j$ in the\nsense of [def-weil-punctual-weights], i.e. $K'\\in D_{\\le w}(X_0)$.",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-complex-weights",
    "lem-a1-mixed-direct-summand",
    "def-weil-punctual-weights"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
